<title>UK: Britain posts record sugar output from 96/97 crop.</title>
<headline>Britain posts record sugar output from 96/97 crop.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain produced a record 1.48 million tonnes of sugar in white value terms from its 1996/97 beet crop, an official at British Sugar said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The previous record was in 1992/93, when around 1,000 tonnes less sugar was produced, the official said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
